# Default lockme PAM stack: minimal, auditable, distribution-independent.
#
# This file contains an explicit auth chain of pam_faildelay (bruteforce
# friction without account lockout) plus pam_unix (password check).
#
# This is the right choice for users who authenticate with a plain Unix
# password. It does NOT support:
#   - systemd-homed (pam_systemd_home)
#   - GNOME Keyring / KWallet auto-unlock
#   - fingerprint readers (pam_fprintd)
#   - smartcards / yubikeys (pam_pkcs11, pam_u2f)
#   - any other auxiliary auth method configured in system-auth
#
# If you need any of the above, install pam.d/lockme.full instead, which
# delegates to the distribution's system-auth chain. See the README's
# "PAM stack" section for details.

auth        optional      pam_faildelay.so delay=2000000
auth        required      pam_unix.so     nullok

account     required      pam_unix.so
